course: dictionary
lesson: 6377
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word mugging is a good example. «Not all bullying is loud: freezing someone out on purpose is bullying too, and a mugging is a crime, not a test of courage.» Here a mugging is a crime, so it means an attack where someone is robbed.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in a different sentence. Sam says, «I am mugging for the camera!» Nobody is being robbed there. Mugging means pulling silly faces, because the camera is the clue. Always ask: what does the rest of the sentence tell me?
explain: The sentence also gives safety advice. «Handing over trainers to stay safe is smart, because things can be replaced and you can't.» It means that your safety matters more than your things. Staying safe is the most important part of the lesson, so remember it well.
fact: A mugging is a crime in a public place, where someone is robbed, often with threats or violence.
fact: Mugging is also the -ing form of «mug», which means to rob someone.
fact: «Mugging for the camera» is an informal phrase that means pulling silly faces.
fact: «Mugging up» is informal British English for studying hard in a short time, which is called cramming.
fact: Safety tip: stay with a group, stay in well-lit places, give up your things rather than fight, and tell an adult or the police.
exercise: What is a mugging, according to the sentence? | A test of courage | *A crime | A game for friends | A kind of bullying that is loud
exercise: Sam says, «I am mugging for the camera!» What is he doing? | Running a race | Reading a map | *Pulling silly faces | Robbing a shop
exercise: Maya says, «I am mugging up for my spelling test tonight.» What is she doing? | Robbing a bag | *Studying hard quickly | Making silly faces | Going to bed early
test: «Handing over trainers to stay safe is smart.» Why does the sentence say this is smart? | Because trainers are expensive | *Because things can be replaced and you can't | Because the thief will say thank you | Because trainers make you run faster
test: Which word means to rob someone? | Muggy, meaning hot and damp | *Mug | Mugging, as a noun for a crime | Muddle
exam: If someone threatens you in a public place, what is the safest choice? | Fight back to protect your phone | *Give up your phone and tell an adult or the police | Stay quiet and say nothing to anyone | Walk alone in a dark alley so you are not seen
